From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:28:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: dma: apple,sio: Add S8000
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9 (S8000/S8003) SmartIO is the same AppleA7IOP coprocessor and
message protocol as on T8010, with its own firmware image. Add its
compatible and an optional reset: the PMGR power state of the
coprocessor resets it when the boot chain left it running.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux c037b6f7 (J71t ledger 10.3); dropped the
 apple,dma-endpoints property: the endpoint set is per-SoC firmware
 knowledge and comes from the driver's match data instead.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml    | 26 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
index 085d29872..8dc7114af 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
@@ -4,13 +4,13 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/dma/apple,sio.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple T8010 SmartIO coprocessor and DMA controller
+title: Apple S8000/T8010 SmartIO coprocessor and DMA controller
 
 description: |
-  The T8010 SmartIO coprocessor provides DMA channels for peripheral
-  controllers. The application processor boots the SmartIO firmware and
-  submits DMA commands through the SIO message queues. Clients select the
-  firmware endpoint number used by their peripheral.
+  The S8000 (A9) and T8010 (A10) SmartIO coprocessor provides DMA channels
+  for peripheral controllers. The application processor boots the SmartIO
+  firmware and submits DMA commands through the SIO message queues. Clients
+  select the firmware endpoint number used by their peripheral.
 
 maintainers:
   - Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
@@ -20,11 +20,13 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: apple,t8010-sio
+    enum:
+      - apple,s8000-sio
+      - apple,t8010-sio
 
   reg:
     items:
-      - description: AppleA7IOPV2 coprocessor and message queue registers
+      - description: AppleA7IOP coprocessor and message queue registers
       - description: SmartIO DMA shim registers
 
   reg-names:
@@ -36,11 +38,17 @@ properties:
     minItems: 4
     maxItems: 4
     description:
-      The four interrupt outputs described by the T8010 SIO device tree node.
+      The four interrupt outputs of the SIO node in the Apple device tree, in
+      the same order.
 
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Power-state reset, used if the coprocessor is found already running.
+
   firmware-name:
     maxItems: 1
 
@@ -51,7 +59,7 @@ properties:
     const: 1
     description:
       Clients specify the SmartIO DMA endpoint number, for example 0x1a for
-      SPI3 transmit and 0x1b for SPI3 receive.
+      SPI3 transmit, 0x1b for SPI3 receive or 0x28 for MCA0 transmit.
 
 required:
   - compatible
